POW.SYSTEMS FRONTIER FEED PROBE =E2=80=94 20 Sep 2026 19:08 ICT

EXECUTIVE DELTA

Highest-information discovery this run: a new GB-wide outage-data
standard is becoming operational across DNOs. UK Power Networks
announced its National Energy Outage API on 6 Aug 2026. Its feed is
sourced from ADMS, includes planned and unplanned outages, follows the
ENA National Energy Outage API design, updates every 15 minutes,
suppresses incidents affecting <=3D5 customers where they cannot be
aggregated, and is CC-BY-4.0. Electricity North West also exposes
NEO-format state every 15 minutes; evidence now indicates all six GB
DNOs have reusable live incident feeds, although licensing/access
differs. This is exactly POW state: place =C3=97 physical network =C3=97 ou=
tage
=C3=97 customers affected =C3=97 restoration time =C3=97 time. Promote GB O=
UTAGE TAPE
to PLANT/PILOT with UKPN as the clean first collector and expand
network-by-network only after licence verification.

Second discovery: UKPN=E2=80=99s Constraints Real Time Meter Readings is a
much stronger physical constraint sensor than generic grid queue data.
It exposes constraint_id, current amps, trim/release limits, breach
flag and timestamp, refreshing approximately once per minute. It
directly measures when physical transformers/cables approach or cross
curtailment limits. This is not newly launched this week, so it is not
a frontier-launch win, but it is a high-value unresolved seed. Future
development will add reasons for non-constraint-driven curtailment;
schema monitoring should start now.

Third discovery: DEFRA Digital Waste Tracking is a major t=3D0 WATCHLIST
event. Public beta opened 28 Apr 2026; mandatory receipt reporting
starts 1 Oct 2026 in England/Wales and Jan 2027 Scotland/NI. The
Receipt API is public-beta v1.1, with seven endpoints and an official
OpenAPI spec. But movement records are authenticated operational data,
not a public read feed. POW must NOT pretend this is collectable.
Watch for future public aggregate/open-data outputs; the mandate is
creating a genuinely new national physical-material movement graph
from Oct 2026.

Fourth: UK Fuel Finder is a genuine 2026 machine-readable mandate:
launched 2 Feb 2026, all forecourts must report price changes within
30 minutes, with current price, operator/brand, amenities and
timestamps available via API/CSV. However third parties already
preserve daily per-forecourt history back to 16 Feb 2026 for free.
Reject generic daily mirroring. Only sub-daily price-transition
capture remains potentially differentiated.

